==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{af|en|allo-|-phone}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈæləˌfəʊn/|lang=en}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/ˈæləˌfoʊn/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|phonology}} Any of two or more alternative pronunciations for a [[phoneme]].
# {{lb|en|Canada}} A person whose [[mother tongue]] is neither English nor French.
# {{lb|en|Canada}} A person whose [[mother tongue]] is one other than that spoken by the majority.

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# {{lb|en|Canada}} That which is of a language neither English nor French.
# {{lb|en|Canada}} That which is of a language other than that spoken by the majority.

